   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Self-attested RC photocopy: Every commercial vehicle involved in the shipment must carry a clear, self-attested copy of its registration certificate. This document verifies vehicle ownership and legal roadworthiness, enabling smooth checkpoint inspections along the Karnataka to Odisha corridor.</span></li>
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Current PUC: A valid Pollution Under Control certificate is mandatory for all transport vehicles. Regulatory authorities frequently verify emission compliance during interstate transit, and an expired PUC can result in hefty fines or shipment holds.</span></li>
   <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Valid insurance certificate: Comprehensive vehicle insurance must be active and readily available. This covers third-party liabilities and basic transit risks, forming the foundational layer of protection for your cargo during the long-distance haul.</span></li>
